-The adaptive controller still prepares each distinct order independently; callers
+The default adaptive controller still prepares each distinct order independently; callers
 can explicitly reuse a prepared higher order for their own finite portfolios.
+
+
+To reuse preparation automatically during adaptive integration, select
+`field.adaptive_taylor(options).share_preparation()` and call its `integrate`.
+The shared outcome's `report()` borrows the complete source-bound adaptive history,
+including rejected quality attempts, certified prefixes and whole-run status.
+The first demanded order is prepared normally; later missing orders extend the
+existing exact coefficient prefix. Maximum order is never prepared eagerly.
+The independent controller remains available with its original work accounting.
+Sharing changes preparation work, retained allocation and exhaustion points, so
+replay must retain this explicit strategy choice with the source/options/request.
+`FlowTaylorProgram::extend_order(additional, &mut budget)` also exposes bounded
+incremental preparation directly; its argument is an additional order count.
+Run `cargo run -p hyperdynamics --features adaptive-taylor --example adaptive_shared`.
